## Secret-Safe Integration Workflow

RULES:
  - Secret values never enter source control, Redis, THINK, DTHINK, logs, prompts, screenshots, or PR comments.
  - Agents report secret names and configured/missing status only.
  - Production values come from the hosting provider secret manager.
  - Local values come from ignored .env files loaded by standalone scripts.
  - Redis MCP is an operational data interface, not a credential vault.
  - Upstash Box uses UPSTASH_BOX_API_KEY from the environment only.

COMMANDS:
  npm run verify:secrets  -> name-only presence and tracked-file leak gate
  npm run verify:box-web  -> Box HTTP staging check when the Box key exists
  node scripts/dthink-pipeline.mjs feed security:policy <safe-summary>
  node scripts/think-forge-bridge.mjs inject secret-safe-integration-workflow

FAILURE POLICY:
  Missing optional credentials are warnings.
  Missing production credentials are failures in strict mode.
  Any tracked credential pattern blocks the gate.
